      "id": "GRA-A1-09",
      "module": "grammar",
      "cefr_target": "A1",
      "title": "This, that, these and those",
      "estimated_minutes": 22,
      "prerequisite_lesson_ids": [
        "GRA-A1-04"
      ],
      "adaptive_concepts": [
        "demonstratives",
        "singular-plural-reference"
      ],
      "objectives": [
        "Choose this/that for one thing and these/those for more than one thing.",
        "Use near/far context to select an appropriate demonstrative.",
        "Match demonstratives with singular or plural nouns."
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "en": "Use this and these for things near the speaker; use that and those for things farther away. This/that are singular: this book, that chair. These/those are plural: these books, those chairs. A demonstrative can stand before a noun or replace the noun when the meaning is clear: These are mine. Distance depends on the situation, so look for clues such as here, in my hand, over there or across the room.",
        "vi": "Dùng this/these cho vật ở gần; that/those cho vật ở xa hơn. This/that đi với số ít; these/those đi với số nhiều. Chú ý các dấu hiệu như here, in my hand, over there."
      },
      "examples": [
        "NEAR ONE · This pencil in my hand is blue.",
        "FAR ONE · That bus over there is ours.",
        "NEAR MANY · These books here are new.",
        "FAR MANY · Those lights across the street are bright."
      ],
