      "id": "GRA-A1-10",
      "module": "grammar",
      "cefr_target": "A1",
      "title": "Object pronouns and possessive pronouns",
      "estimated_minutes": 24,
      "prerequisite_lesson_ids": [
        "GRA-A1-02"
      ],
      "adaptive_concepts": [
        "object-pronouns",
        "possessive-pronouns"
      ],
      "objectives": [
        "Use me/you/him/her/it/us/them after verbs and prepositions.",
        "Use mine/yours/his/hers/ours/theirs without a following noun.",
        "Distinguish possessive adjectives such as my/your from possessive pronouns such as mine/yours."
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "en": "Object pronouns receive the action or follow a preposition: Please help me; I sit next to her; The teacher gives us homework. Possessive pronouns show ownership without a following noun: This book is mine; Those bags are theirs. Do not put a noun after mine/yours/hers/ours/theirs. Compare: This is my pen. The pen is mine.",
        "vi": "Đại từ tân ngữ đứng sau động từ hoặc giới từ: help me, sit next to her. Đại từ sở hữu đứng độc lập, không có danh từ theo sau: mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs."
      },
      "examples": [
        "OBJECT · I know Mia. I sit next to her.",
        "OBJECT · The coach calls us.",
        "POSSESSION · This notebook is mine.",
        "CONTRAST · That is your bag. The bag is yours."
      ],
      "activities": [
