      "objectives": [
        "Use the base verb for positive instructions.",
        "Form negative instructions with don't + base verb.",
        "Recognise polite and clearly ordered everyday instructions."
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "en": "Use the base form of a verb to give an instruction: Open the window. Add please to make a request sound more polite: Please sit down. For a negative instruction, use don't + base verb: Don't touch the screen. The subject you is normally understood and not written. For steps, words such as first, then and finally can make the order clear.",
        "vi": "Dùng động từ nguyên mẫu để ra hướng dẫn: Open the book. Phủ định dùng don't + động từ nguyên mẫu: Don't run. Có thể thêm please để lịch sự hơn và first/then/finally để sắp xếp các bước."
      },
      "examples": [
        "POSITIVE · Turn left at the corner.",
        "POLITE · Please close the door.",
        "NEGATIVE · Don't run in the hallway.",
        "SEQUENCE · First wash the fruit. Then cut it."
      ],
